GOLD SILVER MONEY

Algoron's economy is based on gold and silver coinage (and the lowly copper,
which you as an adventurer are far too proud to carry).  Gold coins are
worth 100 silver coins, but are also four times as heavy (25 to the pound,
as opposed to 100 to the pound for silver).

Gems can be bought from different jewelers to alleviate weight problems,
they charge a mere 10% more than they are worth.  10 gems weigh one pound,
and they can be worth more than 100 gold pieces for the highest quality
stones.

Another means of preventing problems from the weight of your treasure is by
exchanging silver for gold.  There is a money-changer in most kingdoms.

The most valuable jewel in Algoron is a jeweled egg.  These may be bought
from any shopkeeper with the purchase command, see help purchase.

To prevent the loss of any treasure you have amassed, jeweled eggs may be
deposited with the banker in different kingdoms.  They are so wealthy that
they only deal in eggs, no other form of currency may be deposited.

Various kingdoms about the realm charge a degree of tax that will change the
exact price of exchange for diamonds that you may purchase.  It would
beenefit you to pay attention to those taxes when making a purchase.  There
are some areas about the realm that may be tax free.

   100 silver =   1 gold  =  0 diamonds       = 0 eggs
 11000 silver = 110 gold  =  1 diamond        = 0 jeweled egg
 55000 silver = 550 gold  =  1 blue diamond   = 0.1 jeweled egg
550000 silver = 5500 gold = 10 blue diamonds  = 1 jeweled egg

